      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This sounds serious; because your child hasn't had a wet diaper in 6–7 hours and seems very tired, call your pediatrician immediately or go to the ER right away. At home, you could offer small, frequent sips of an oral rehydration solution (Pedialyte) instead of juice or sports drinks, but only after seeking medical advice first. Do not force fluids or give anti-nausea medications without a doctor's specific instruction, as rapid rehydration attempts can sometimes trigger more vomiting.",
