      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No, you should not use salt tablets or make your own homemade electrolyte mix because incorrect ratios can lead to serious and life-threatening imbalances like hypernatremia or water intoxication, which are especially dangerous for a tired 2-year-old. Waiting even a few more hours without proper medical guidance is risky given his symptoms of excessive tiredness and lack of urination, so booking the ER appointment immediately is the safest way to get the professional care he likely needs. It is better to pay for the drive once and likely receive better long-term outcomes now than to risk a medical emergency at home.",
